wsVirtualKeyCode, shift) on a US keyboard\n    layout, or (\"\", 0, False) if no US key produces it.\"\"\"\n    if char.isascii() and char.isalpha():\n        return f\"Key{char.upper()}\", ord(char.upper()), char.isupper()\n    if char.isascii() and char.isdigit():\n        return f\"Digit{char}\", ord(char), False\n    if char in _SHIFT_SYMBOLS:\n        code, vk = _SHIFT_SYMBOLS[char]\n        return code, vk, True\n    if char in _UNSHIFTED_SYMBOLS:\n        code, vk = _UNSHIFTED_SYMBOLS[char]\n        return code, vk, False\n    return \"\", 0, False\n\ndef press_key(key, modifiers=0):\n    \"\"\"Modifiers bitfield: 1=Alt, 2=Ctrl, 4=Meta(Cmd), 8=Shift.\n    Special keys (Enter, Tab, Arrow*, Backspace, etc.) carry their virtual key codes\n    so listeners checking e.keyCode / e.key all fire. A single character is mapped to\n    its US-keyboard physical key (code + Shift), or code=\"\" if no US key produces it.\"\"\"\n    if key in _KEYS:\n        vk, code, text = _KEYS[key]\n    elif len(key) == 1:\n        code, vk, shift = _us_layout_key(key)\n        text = key\n        if shift:\n            modifiers |= 8\n    else:\n        vk, code, text = 0, key, \"\"\n    base = {\"key\": key, \"code\": code, \"modifiers\": modifiers, \"windowsVirtualKeyCode\": vk, \"nativeVirtualKeyCode\": vk}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5015,"cache_read_input_tokens":52092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5015},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ad40c43-ed88-42ec-89b7-bb6070252db2","uuid":"37e53a26-5386-4063-8823-acb3e501fdff","timestamp":"2026-09-10T05:27:35.108Z","request_id":"req_011CeuCryaSxABMDQjmtMdJh"}
